{"ts": 1793977911.2834864, "run_id": "bsa_standards__driver_only__claude-haiku-5-5__r1__c5f45421a831", "source": "agent", "event": "assistant_text", "text": "I made 100 \u00b5L each of the three BSA standards in assay_plate wells B1\u2013B3, diluting the 2 mg/mL BSA stock with PBS.\n\n- **B1 (0 mg/mL):** 100 \u00b5L PBS.\n- **B2 (0.5 mg/mL):** 75 \u00b5L PBS + 25 \u00b5L BSA stock.\n- **B3 (1.0 mg/mL):** 50 \u00b5L PBS + 50 \u00b5L BSA stock.\n\nEach transfer used a fresh tip, and all steps reported as executed. The deck volumes match: PBS dropped by 225 \u00b5L (40000 \u2192 39775) and BSA stock by 75 \u00b5L (10000 \u2192 9925). I did not read the plate or check the well contents directly.\n\nOne slip: for the first well I issued the pick-up, aspirate, dispense and drop calls together rather than one at a time. They ran in the correct order and nothing went wrong, but I ran the rest one at a time."}
